  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kenya Agricultural Carbon Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall project objective is carbon sequestration through the adoption of sustainable agricultural land management practices inWestern Kenya.The project entity, the NGO ViAgroforestry (ViA) is promoting the adoption of SALM practices on approximately 45,000ha in Nyanza and Western Provinces. Expected outcomes include that smallholder farmers in Kenya will be able to access the carbon market and receive additional carbon revenue streams through the adoption of productivity enhancing practices and technologies.</narrative>
  </description>
